*(Note: I also fixed a couple of small array indexing bugs from the earlier draft—like `PICO8_PALETTE` colors and `files[0]`—so the sprite colors render accurately in Safari.)*

---

### 2. Sample `testrom.p8` (Place right next to `index.html`)
This is a valid, playable PICO-8 cartridge featuring **4 distinct `8×8` pixel sprites** (a cute Pico-cat character, a grass/dirt ground block, a golden coin, and a spike hazard), a **`16×16` starter tilemap**, and working **platformer movement Lua code** so you can also open `testrom.p8` directly in `pico-8-edu.com` to compare the original and your `.sb3` remaster side by side!

```text
pico-8 cartridge // http://www.pico-8.com
version 42
__lua__
-- testrom.p8: mini pico-cat demo
px = 24
py = 80
vx = 0
vy = 0
grounded = false

function _update()
  vx = 0
  if (btn(0)) vx = -1.5
  if (btn(1)) vx = 1.5
  if (btnp(4) and grounded) then
    vy = -3.6
    grounded = false
  end

  vy += 0.25
  px += vx
  py += vy

  if (py >= 96) then
    py = 96
    vy = 0
    grounded = true
  end
end

function _draw()
  cls(12)
  map(0, 0, 0, 0, 16, 16)
  spr(1, px, py)
  spr(3, 88, 88)
  print("testrom.p8", 44, 8, 7)
end
